{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789314266,"nonce":"sCqqdXNY92rHHz9Xv3xcz+gK96s=","title":"Cranelift's leaf loop issues ~1.7x LLVM's instructions per iteration on the call benches","message":"Per-iteration listing for `sum = sum*31 + (i%8)` (bench_free_call /\nbench_inlined_call), from the CLIF and the live JIT code under lldb on\naarch64 and llc on the dumped IR for x86-64: Cranelift 21-23 instructions\n(~20 on x86-64, 2 loads) against LLVM's 10 (13 on x86-64, 1 load). The\ndependency chain is the same 3 cycles in both (`const_mul` already emits\n`(x\u003c\u003c5)-x`), and on the M1 both run at the 3-cycle floor (cycle counters:\n~3.0/iter each), so the extra instructions cost nothing there. On the NUC\n(i5-1250P) the Cranelift OSR entry runs ~87ms against ash-aot's 70ms,\nwhich is itself the 3-cycle floor at 4.4GHz (68ms) -- so the extra\ninstructions cost ~1.2x on x86-64, not more.\n\nWhere the extra instructions are, largest first:\n1. `i % 8` -- `const_div` (codegen.rs ~2853-2874) emits the sign-correct\n   5-op sequence `asr 31, lsr 29, add, and 7, sub`; LLVM proves `i \u003e= 0`\n   (IndVars `nuw nsw` + CVP) and emits one `and 7`. A non-negative\n   induction check turning `SMod` by 2^k into `band_imm`, in Cranelift's\n   `const_div` or as an AIR pass so every engine agrees.\n2. The fiber poll (codegen.rs ~1083-1121) keeps the handled epoch in a\n   stack slot and reloads it every iteration (LLVM carries it in a phi),\n   and the epoch's 64-bit address is an `iconst` the egraph rematerializes\n   inside the loop. An SSA `Variable` for the epoch and a non-`iconst`\n   address.\n3. Two regalloc2 block-parameter copies per iteration (mov-eliminated on\n   most cores).\n4. inlined_call only: a dead store to the address-taken `sum` cell every\n   iteration, because cellfwd (passes/cellfwd.rs ~84) treats the may-trap\n   `SMod` as a barrier; Cranelift's alias analysis forwards the load but\n   the store stays.\n\nThe retier poll is no longer in the loop (it rides the fiber poll's cold\nedge), so the listing above is the whole per-iteration difference.","files":null}]}